        <item>
            <title>0.9.14</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:26:22 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>20261028.2326</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.9.14</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:12px}h1,h2{font-size:15px}</style><h2>Kaiju 0.9.14 beta</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Smart Transpose, checked on a KRONOS:</b> the slot transpose applies after the key zones, so splits and cheat notes are fine and no longer warned about. What's left to watch:
<ul>
<li><b>drum kits</b> play other drums. <b>Fix: a copy for this slot</b> makes a copy of the combi ("Name -3") with only its drum kits transposed the other way, so every key plays its own drum again. Programs and key zones never change.
</li>
<li><b>one sample per key</b> multisamples and <b>wave sequences</b> are listed to check by ear; tick <b>Fix too</b> to transpose them back in the same copy.
</li></ul>
</li>
<li><b>Set list slots:</b>
<ul>
<li>transpose goes to ±24, like the KRONOS;
</li>
<li>a slot with no name but a sound plays on the keyboard, so Kaiju keeps it when importing, copying and moving sounds, and shows it as "(no name)";
</li>
<li><b>Empty set list…</b> works on any set list that isn't factory-fresh, and is also in a ⋯ menu above the slots.
</li></ul>
</li>
<li><b>Preview:</b> note sizes XS, S and L measured on the keyboard.
</li>
<li><b>The TXT saved with a PCG</b> now reads like a guide:
<ul>
<li>what the file replaces on your KRONOS (whole banks; partly used banks load the rest empty);
</li>
<li>how to load it step by step with the keyboard's own screen names: a FAT32 USB stick, a Save All backup first, samples before the PCG, then everything, one part, one bank or one sound;
</li>
<li>a checklist;
</li>
<li>a slot-by-slot list of what's new, moved or replaced, and which set list slots changed.
</li></ul>
</li>
<li>Muted timbres fade in the timbre editor, like Off ones (they don't sound).
</li>
<li>The sidebar counts follow the PCG after a save (they showed the file as first opened).
</li></ul>]]></description>
