        <item>
            <title>0.9.11</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:14:10 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>20261026.1714</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.9.11</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:12px}h1,h2{font-size:15px}</style><h2>Kaiju 0.9.11 beta</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Set lists look like the KRONOS screen:</b> the yellow bar over the slots shows the slot you're editing (name, sound and notes, before you apply them), slots come 4 per row in their full colors, and the font sizes are XS, S, M, L and XL as the KRONOS stores them.
</li>
<li><b>Preview:</b> the button in a slot's panel shows the slot on the KRONOS' Set List screen, with the notes at the size the keyboard uses and cut where it cuts them. "Hide slot" appears when the notes reach the slot's button.
</li>
<li><b>Tools › Set list slots that play nothing:</b> finds slots pointing at an empty combi or program, or at a user bank this PCG doesn't have, and empties the ones you tick in one step (Undo brings them back).
</li>
<li><b>EXi engines:</b> an EXi program's panel shows its engines (for example SGX-2 + MOD-7), and Organize › Sort › Sort by engine groups an EXi bank by engine. HD-1 / EXi is now called "Bank type".
</li>
<li><b>Drum Track patterns:</b> select several and delete them, or delete the unused ones or all of them.
</li>
<li><b>Import:</b>
<ul>
<li>the bank picker shows where things will go, and choosing another bank moves them there;
